# Henry is king of France. Mary loves Henry. If a man is king of a country, he is successful. If a girl loves a successful man, she is ambitious.

predicate man {theme: e}
predicate girl {theme: e}
predicate king_of {theme: e, reference: e}
predicate country {theme: e}
predicate love {agent: e, patient: e}
predicate successful {theme: e}
predicate ambitious {theme: e}

entity henry : e
entity mary : e
entity france : e

man(theme: henry)
girl(theme: mary)
king_of(theme: henry, reference: france)
country(theme: france)
love(agent: mary, patient: henry)

rule [x:e, c:e]: man(theme: x) & king_of(theme: x, reference: c) & country(theme: c) -> successful(theme: x)
rule [x:e, y:e]: girl(theme: x) & love(agent: x, patient: y) & successful(theme: y) -> ambitious(theme: x)

? ambitious(theme: mary)